## ================================================================
## BOOTEI chi^2 – Sample size savings (butyraldehyde inhalation 2-year study; chunked)
## FIXED-MARGINS (conditional) DGP for 2x2 tables, linear-by-linear (k=2) form
##
## Goal:
##   Estimate sample size savings of BOOTEI vs classical permutation chi^2,
##   for 2x2 control-vs-dose contrasts derived from Furukawa et al. (2024).
##
## Data source (counts used to build observed 2x2 tables):
##   Furukawa Y. et al. (2024) J. Toxicol. Sci. 49(9):385–398
##   "Carcinogenicity of butyraldehyde in rats by a two-year inhalation study"
##
## What is included:
##   - All binary endpoints with explicit incidence counts reported in:
##       * Table 1 (neoplastic lesions)
##       * Table 2 (selected non-neoplastic lesions)
##       * Results text: terminal survival counts
##   - All natural contrasts: 0 ppm vs {300, 1000, 3000} ppm within sex
##
## What is excluded (mechanically, no cherry-picking):
##   1) observed-degenerate 2x2 tables:
##        - total events = 0  (all-zero event column)
##        - total events = N  (all-one event column)
##      because they carry no information for a 2x2 test
##   2) exact duplicate 2x2 tables (same x0/n0 vs x1/n1), even if they come
##      from different endpoints/dose/sex; these are collapsed to one scenario
##   3) historical-control table (Table 3), because it is not a treatment-study
##      control-vs-dose 2x2 comparison from this experiment
##
## Endpoint definition (binary per animal):
##   lesion/tumor present (1) vs absent (0)
##   (for survival rows: "alive at terminal sacrifice" = 1 vs not = 0)
##
## DGP (fixed margins; linear-by-linear k=2; data-anchored, standard):
##   For each observed 2x2 scenario (x0/n0 vs x1/n1), define:
##     p0 = x0/n0, p1 = x1/n1
##
##   For each simulated equal-group size n:
##     - Row margins fixed: n_control = n_treated = n
##     - Column margin fixed (total events) using observed group rates:
##         m(n) = round( (p0 + p1) * n )     (since E[events]=n p0 + n p1)
##       clamped to [0, 2n]
##     - Association parameter uses linear-by-linear k=2 form:
##         P(A=a | n,n,m,theta) ∝ choose(n,a) * choose(n,m-a) * exp(theta * a)
##       where A = treated events.
##     - theta is calibrated (per n) so that:
##         E[A | n,n,m(n),theta] ≈ n * p1
##       i.e., the treated event rate matches the observed p1 under the
##       conditioning constraint (fixed margins).
##
##   This keeps:
##     - fixed margins (matches permutation conditioning on margins),
##     - linear-by-linear model family used in BOOTEI simulations (k=2 case),
##     - and anchoring to the observed control/treatment rates (p0,p1),
##   without relying on unstable OR plug-ins for rare/zero cells.
##
## Degenerate simulated margins:
##   If m(n) in {0, 2n}, outcome is constant -> keep replicate, set p=1 (no rejection)
## ================================================================

